course: dictionary
lesson: 8420
title: Russian: a place, a person, a language
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one job. Russian can describe something, name a person, or name a language. Look at the words around it to find out which job it is doing. In «"Kiev" came from the Russian spelling», Russian describes the spelling, so it means connected with Russia.
explain: Russia is the very large country that stretches from Eastern Europe across northern Asia. Blakiston's fish owl lives in the «Russian Far East», which is a part of that big country. So here Russian describes the place, just as «Russian dolls» describes dolls from that country.
explain: A Russian is a person from Russia, so a Russian can be a noun, and there can be many Russians. Russian can also be a language. You say you speak Russian, with no a in front, because you are naming a language, not a person.
explain: The check is simple: swap in «from Russia» or «a person from Russia». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Russian can describe things from or connected with Russia, such as a Russian spelling or a Russian forest.
fact: A Russian is a person from Russia, and Russians means more than one person.
fact: Russian is also the main language of Russia, and it is written in the Cyrillic alphabet.
fact: Russia is the largest country in the world by area, and it has many time zones.
fact: Russian folk tales include Baba Yaga and the firebird, and Russian dolls called matryoshka fit one inside another.
exercise: «Blakiston's fish owl of the Russian Far East and Japan is one of the heaviest owls.» What does Russian mean here? | A kind of fish | A very cold month | A language spoken in Japan | *Connected with Russia
exercise: What is a Russian? | A type of owl | A kind of nesting doll | *A person from Russia | A river in Japan
exercise: Which alphabet is used to write Russian? | Roman alphabet, like English | Greek alphabet | Arabic script | *Cyrillic alphabet
test: In «"Kiev" came from the Russian spelling», Russian means: | A kind of bird | A person who lives in Kiev | *Connected with Russia | A language used in Ukraine
test: The main language of Russia is also called Russian. What does Russian mean when it names a language? | Something you can eat | Spanish, spoken in many countries | *The main language of Russia, written in Cyrillic | A kind of dance
exam: Which sentence uses Russian to mean a person from Russia? | I speak Russian at school | Russian is my favourite word to say | *The Russian sat by the window and read | The Russian river froze over in winter
